1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,880
Imagine you open your eyes...

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,162
and the whole world is gone.

3
00:00:03,802 --> 00:00:04,834
No houses.

4
00:00:04,890 --> 00:00:05,883
No roads.

5
00:00:05,939 --> 00:00:06,946
No tools.

6
00:00:07,002 --> 00:00:07,940
Not even a knife.

7
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:09,573
Just your body,

8
00:00:09,593 --> 00:00:11,692
and a wild land you know nothing about.

9
00:00:12,332 --> 00:00:13,414
This is Zero.

10
00:00:13,470 --> 00:00:14,937
And today is day one of

11
00:00:14,957 --> 00:00:16,820
rebuilding the world from zero.

12
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,319
So the first question sounds simple.

13
00:00:20,382 --> 00:00:21,412
But get it wrong,

14
00:00:21,432 --> 00:00:22,845
and it could cost your life.

15
00:00:22,895 --> 00:00:24,007
What do you do first?

16
00:00:24,647 --> 00:00:25,541
Find food?

17
00:00:25,597 --> 00:00:26,603
Build a house?

18
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:27,559
Make fire?

19
00:00:27,622 --> 00:00:28,660
They all matter.

20
00:00:28,722 --> 00:00:30,122
But none of them comes first.

21
00:00:30,762 --> 00:00:31,492
Because if you don't

22
00:00:31,512 --> 00:00:32,823
know what's around you,

23
00:00:32,861 --> 00:00:34,824
every decision is just a guess.

24
00:00:35,464 --> 00:00:36,668
So step one is:

25
00:00:36,688 --> 00:00:37,682
know the land.

26
00:00:37,739 --> 00:00:39,193
Where the useful things are,

27
00:00:39,213 --> 00:00:40,401
and where the danger is.

28
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:43,140
Today's goal: before sunset,

29
00:00:43,178 --> 00:00:45,158
Zero has to learn this valley,

30
00:00:45,178 --> 00:00:46,445
and pick one safe place

31
00:00:46,465 --> 00:00:47,678
for his first base.

32
00:00:48,318 --> 00:00:49,181
The catch?

33
00:00:49,243 --> 00:00:50,617
He only has half a day.

34
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,649
His body already needs water.

35
00:00:52,705 --> 00:00:53,817
And he has nothing at all.

36
00:00:55,117 --> 00:00:56,985
Zero starts with what's closest.

37
00:00:57,042 --> 00:00:58,047
Under his feet:

38
00:00:58,067 --> 00:00:59,067
grassland.

39
00:00:59,129 --> 00:01:00,322
The soil is firm,

40
00:01:00,342 --> 00:01:01,117
not soggy.

41
00:01:01,757 --> 00:01:04,126
That means water doesn't pool here much.

42
00:01:04,182 --> 00:01:05,782
A good sign for a place to live.

43
00:01:06,422 --> 00:01:07,953
But the sun is brutal.

44
00:01:08,009 --> 00:01:08,901
In this heat,

45
00:01:08,921 --> 00:01:10,539
the body sweats fast,

46
00:01:10,559 --> 00:01:11,351
and you can dry out

47
00:01:11,371 --> 00:01:12,796
before you even notice.

48
00:01:13,436 --> 00:01:14,828
On a very hot day,

49
00:01:14,848 --> 00:01:16,466
someone working in the sun can sweat

50
00:01:16,486 --> 00:01:18,098
out more than a liter an hour.

51
00:01:18,738 --> 00:01:21,213
The early warning signs of dehydration:

52
00:01:21,238 --> 00:01:22,868
thirst, a headache,

53
00:01:22,888 --> 00:01:23,713
and dark urine.

54
00:01:24,353 --> 00:01:25,560
Zero makes a note.

55
00:01:25,616 --> 00:01:26,828
Water is urgent.

56
00:01:26,891 --> 00:01:28,045
But first, he needs

57
00:01:28,065 --> 00:01:29,465
to know which way is which.

58
00:01:30,105 --> 00:01:31,611
He picks up a straight stick.

59
00:01:31,667 --> 00:01:32,947
It's not a tool yet,

60
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:34,267
but it can tell him direction.

61
00:01:34,907 --> 00:01:35,874
He pushes the stick

62
00:01:35,894 --> 00:01:37,361
upright into the ground,

63
00:01:37,381 --> 00:01:38,511
and puts a small pebble

64
00:01:38,531 --> 00:01:39,882
at the tip of its shadow.

65
00:01:40,522 --> 00:01:42,146
The sun rises in the east

66
00:01:42,221 --> 00:01:43,703
and sets in the west.

67
00:01:43,759 --> 00:01:44,676
Wait a while,

68
00:01:44,696 --> 00:01:46,784
and the tip of the shadow slowly moves.

69
00:01:47,584 --> 00:01:48,689
He puts a second pebble

70
00:01:48,709 --> 00:01:50,178
at the new shadow tip.

71
00:01:50,234 --> 00:01:51,564
A line from the first pebble to

72
00:01:51,584 --> 00:01:53,934
the second points roughly west to east.

73
00:01:54,574 --> 00:01:56,442
Once you know east and west,

74
00:01:56,462 --> 00:01:57,956
north and south follow.

75
00:01:58,012 --> 00:02:00,399
Now Zero has a compass made by the sun.

76
00:02:01,039 --> 00:02:01,956
The problem is,

77
00:02:01,976 --> 00:02:04,019
from down here he can't see far.

78
00:02:04,076 --> 00:02:05,656
Tall grass and trees block

79
00:02:05,676 --> 00:02:07,076
almost every direction.

80
00:02:07,716 --> 00:02:09,391
To understand the whole valley,

81
00:02:09,441 --> 00:02:11,078
he has to look from somewhere high.

82
00:02:11,718 --> 00:02:14,335
Zero walks to a huge boulder to the north,

83
00:02:14,355 --> 00:02:15,773
and carefully climbs up,

84
00:02:15,793 --> 00:02:16,943
one step at a time.

85
00:02:17,583 --> 00:02:18,513
And from up here,

86
00:02:18,533 --> 00:02:20,033
the whole valley opens up.

87
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:23,013
Before he explores further,

88
00:02:23,070 --> 00:02:24,512
let's look at the rule survival

89
00:02:24,532 --> 00:02:26,776
experts use to set priorities.

90
00:02:26,833 --> 00:02:28,420
It's called the rule of threes.

91
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:30,265
A person can last about

92
00:02:30,285 --> 00:02:31,927
three minutes without air,

93
00:02:31,947 --> 00:02:33,427
and about three hours in harsh

94
00:02:33,447 --> 00:02:34,685
weather without shelter.

95
00:02:35,325 --> 00:02:37,205
About three days without water,

96
00:02:37,225 --> 00:02:39,187
and about three weeks without food.

97
00:02:39,827 --> 00:02:40,744
But in heat,

98
00:02:40,764 --> 00:02:41,732
with hard work,

99
00:02:41,752 --> 00:02:43,094
the body runs out of water

100
00:02:43,114 --> 00:02:44,489
much faster than that.

101
00:02:45,129 --> 00:02:47,134
These numbers are only rough estimates,

102
00:02:47,154 --> 00:02:48,367
not hard rules.

103
00:02:48,429 --> 00:02:49,197
But they make it very

104
00:02:49,217 --> 00:02:50,654
clear what's most urgent.

105
00:02:51,294 --> 00:02:52,894
Zero already has air.

106
00:02:52,956 --> 00:02:55,056
So next come shelter and water.

107
00:02:55,132 --> 00:02:55,869
Food can wait.

108
00:02:56,509 --> 00:02:58,052
And both shelter and water

109
00:02:58,072 --> 00:02:59,615
start with the same question:

110
00:02:59,659 --> 00:03:00,259
where?

111
00:03:00,699 --> 00:03:01,767
Good shelter is close

112
00:03:01,787 --> 00:03:03,267
enough to walk to water,

113
00:03:03,287 --> 00:03:05,655
but not so close the water can flood it.

114
00:03:05,711 --> 00:03:07,449
And near the materials you'll build with.

115
00:03:08,089 --> 00:03:09,781
A good way to explore is to split

116
00:03:09,801 --> 00:03:11,344
the land into directions,

117
00:03:11,364 --> 00:03:12,744
and ask every direction

118
00:03:12,764 --> 00:03:14,251
the same three questions.

119
00:03:14,891 --> 00:03:16,072
What here is useful?

120
00:03:16,128 --> 00:03:17,248
What here can hurt me?

121
00:03:17,304 --> 00:03:18,633
And if something goes wrong,

122
00:03:18,653 --> 00:03:19,666
which way do I run?

123
00:03:20,306 --> 00:03:22,744
That last one is the one people forget.

124
00:03:22,806 --> 00:03:24,099
But it matters most,

125
00:03:24,119 --> 00:03:26,024
because when danger really comes,

126
00:03:26,044 --> 00:03:27,381
there's no time to think.

127
00:03:28,681 --> 00:03:29,511
To the north,

128
00:03:29,531 --> 00:03:31,474
the valley opens into plains,

129
00:03:31,494 --> 00:03:33,011
with a river winding all

130
00:03:33,031 --> 00:03:34,718
the way to distant mountains.

131
00:03:35,358 --> 00:03:36,787
But Zero spots a huge

132
00:03:36,807 --> 00:03:38,301
dark cloud to the right.

133
00:03:38,357 --> 00:03:39,850
Rain here could come fast,

134
00:03:39,870 --> 00:03:40,495
and heavy.

135
00:03:41,135 --> 00:03:41,978
To the west:

136
00:03:41,998 --> 00:03:43,079
thick jungle.

137
00:03:43,135 --> 00:03:45,566
Wood, vines, and big leaves.

138
00:03:45,623 --> 00:03:47,160
A great source of materials.

139
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,906
But in the jungle you can't see far,

140
00:03:49,950 --> 00:03:51,467
it's easy to get lost,

141
00:03:51,487 --> 00:03:53,337
and there may be animals you can't see.

142
00:03:53,977 --> 00:03:54,882
To the east:

143
00:03:54,902 --> 00:03:56,071
a wide river.

144
00:03:56,127 --> 00:03:58,152
Water, stones, and gravel.

145
00:03:58,792 --> 00:04:00,659
But a river also has currents,

146
00:04:00,679 --> 00:04:01,496
and a water level

147
00:04:01,516 --> 00:04:02,754
that can change with the rain.

148
00:04:03,394 --> 00:04:04,424
And to the south,

149
00:04:04,444 --> 00:04:07,423
a long, tall cliff stands like a wall,

150
00:04:07,443 --> 00:04:09,131
with a green hill in front of it.

151
00:04:09,771 --> 00:04:11,609
Cliffs give shade and stone.

152
00:04:11,671 --> 00:04:13,484
But rocks can also fall from above.

153
00:04:14,124 --> 00:04:16,048
Now Zero has the big picture.

154
00:04:16,111 --> 00:04:17,716
The next step is to go down

155
00:04:17,736 --> 00:04:19,324
and check each place for real.

156
00:04:19,964 --> 00:04:21,632
Zero memorizes the view,

157
00:04:21,652 --> 00:04:22,833
and plans a route.

158
00:04:22,889 --> 00:04:24,831
West first, then east,

159
00:04:24,851 --> 00:04:26,232
then around to the south,

160
00:04:26,252 --> 00:04:27,926
before the hottest part of the day.

161
00:04:29,226 --> 00:04:31,969
First stop: the jungle edge in the west.

162
00:04:32,026 --> 00:04:33,425
Vines hang everywhere.

163
00:04:33,488 --> 00:04:34,570
He gives one a pull.

164
00:04:34,626 --> 00:04:35,426
Really strong.

165
00:04:36,066 --> 00:04:37,083
Vines like these could be

166
00:04:37,103 --> 00:04:38,885
used for tying things later.

167
00:04:38,941 --> 00:04:40,379
Zero remembers this spot.

168
00:04:41,019 --> 00:04:43,431
There's a bush full of bright red berries.

169
00:04:43,493 --> 00:04:44,706
They look delicious.

170
00:04:44,768 --> 00:04:46,268
But Zero stops his hand.

171
00:04:46,908 --> 00:04:48,958
Unknown fruit can be poisonous.

172
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,058
The simple rule:

173
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,863
if you're not one hundred percent sure,

174
00:04:51,883 --> 00:04:52,583
don't eat it.

175
00:04:53,223 --> 00:04:54,402
Deeper in the jungle,

176
00:04:54,422 --> 00:04:56,504
light barely reaches the ground.

177
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:58,273
Every direction looks the same.

178
00:04:58,913 --> 00:05:00,681
Zero snaps small branches

179
00:05:00,701 --> 00:05:01,881
so they hang down,

180
00:05:01,901 --> 00:05:03,107
every so often.

181
00:05:03,164 --> 00:05:04,726
Markers to find his way back.

182
00:05:05,366 --> 00:05:06,908
Without markers, on the way

183
00:05:06,928 --> 00:05:09,216
back every tree looks the same.

184
00:05:09,278 --> 00:05:11,108
People get lost in forests even

185
00:05:11,128 --> 00:05:12,916
when the way out isn't far at all.

186
00:05:13,556 --> 00:05:15,956
Second stop: the river in the east.

187
00:05:16,018 --> 00:05:17,248
The water is slow,

188
00:05:17,268 --> 00:05:19,261
shallow, and so clear you can see

189
00:05:19,281 --> 00:05:20,443
the pebbles on the bottom.

190
00:05:21,083 --> 00:05:22,938
Zero is really thirsty,

191
00:05:22,958 --> 00:05:24,376
but he doesn't drink yet.

192
00:05:24,433 --> 00:05:25,995
Clear water looks safe.

193
00:05:26,058 --> 00:05:27,646
But that still needs to be proven.

194
00:05:28,286 --> 00:05:29,766
Further upstream, the water

195
00:05:29,786 --> 00:05:31,579
gets faster and stronger,

196
00:05:31,623 --> 00:05:33,661
until it turns into white rapids.

197
00:05:34,301 --> 00:05:35,656
The water is so loud you

198
00:05:35,676 --> 00:05:37,769
can barely hear anything else.

199
00:05:37,826 --> 00:05:39,580
The rocks at the edge are wet,

200
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:41,238
and covered in slippery algae.

201
00:05:41,878 --> 00:05:43,433
Fast water only knee deep

202
00:05:43,453 --> 00:05:45,359
can already knock a person over.

203
00:05:45,416 --> 00:05:46,934
This is no place to go in.

204
00:05:46,991 --> 00:05:47,591
Ever.

205
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:49,222
Along the other bank,

206
00:05:49,242 --> 00:05:50,486
the ground is clay.

207
00:05:50,542 --> 00:05:51,410
Step on it,

208
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:52,322
and you slip,

209
00:05:52,342 --> 00:05:53,705
and sink to your ankles.

210
00:05:54,345 --> 00:05:55,437
But clay like this could

211
00:05:55,457 --> 00:05:57,144
be very useful one day.

212
00:05:57,207 --> 00:05:58,824
So Zero marks it in his mind,

213
00:05:58,844 --> 00:05:59,444
too.

214
00:05:59,910 --> 00:06:01,152
Third stop: the foot

215
00:06:01,172 --> 00:06:02,459
of the southern cliff.

216
00:06:02,522 --> 00:06:04,490
The rocks here come in many colors.

217
00:06:04,547 --> 00:06:05,435
Some are deep red.

218
00:06:06,075 --> 00:06:07,005
Zero doesn't know what

219
00:06:07,025 --> 00:06:08,562
these red rocks are yet.

220
00:06:08,625 --> 00:06:09,667
But a color that's different

221
00:06:09,687 --> 00:06:11,225
from the rocks around it often

222
00:06:11,250 --> 00:06:13,288
means some mineral is mixed in.

223
00:06:13,928 --> 00:06:15,208
The broken rock piled up

224
00:06:15,228 --> 00:06:16,657
at the bottom of the cliff tells

225
00:06:16,677 --> 00:06:18,490
him rocks fall from up there,

226
00:06:18,528 --> 00:06:19,728
again and again.

227
00:06:20,368 --> 00:06:21,660
So Zero doesn't stand

228
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:23,105
under the cliff for long,

229
00:06:23,143 --> 00:06:24,197
and notices how far

230
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:25,755
the big rocks have rolled.

231
00:06:25,817 --> 00:06:26,880
That's the danger zone.

232
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,987
Walking along the cliff,

233
00:06:29,007 --> 00:06:30,994
Zero finds a rock shelter,

234
00:06:31,032 --> 00:06:33,344
an overhang sticking out like a roof.

235
00:06:33,984 --> 00:06:35,934
A natural place to hide from rain.

236
00:06:35,997 --> 00:06:37,602
But first, he has to check if

237
00:06:37,622 --> 00:06:39,209
an animal already lives here.

238
00:06:39,849 --> 00:06:41,254
There are animal tracks,

239
00:06:41,274 --> 00:06:43,011
and fur stuck on the rocks.

240
00:06:43,074 --> 00:06:44,880
This place already has an owner.

241
00:06:44,937 --> 00:06:46,624
Zero quietly backs away.

242
00:06:47,924 --> 00:06:49,136
It's late afternoon.

243
00:06:49,187 --> 00:06:51,593
Zero needs to choose a place for his base.

244
00:06:51,649 --> 00:06:53,386
And he finds one that looks perfect.

245
00:06:54,026 --> 00:06:55,751
A sandbar at the river bend.

246
00:06:55,839 --> 00:06:57,518
Flat ground, soft,

247
00:06:57,538 --> 00:06:58,707
close to water,

248
00:06:58,738 --> 00:07:00,351
and full of driftwood to use.

249
00:07:00,991 --> 00:07:02,183
It looks like the best place

250
00:07:02,203 --> 00:07:03,779
for a base in the whole valley.

251
00:07:04,419 --> 00:07:05,336
He lies there listening

252
00:07:05,356 --> 00:07:06,693
to the gentle water,

253
00:07:06,719 --> 00:07:08,387
and thinks: tonight,

254
00:07:08,431 --> 00:07:09,631
I'm sleeping right here.

255
00:07:10,271 --> 00:07:11,426
Until he looks up,

256
00:07:11,446 --> 00:07:12,676
and sees dry grass

257
00:07:12,696 --> 00:07:14,451
and sticks caught in a bush,

258
00:07:14,471 --> 00:07:15,746
higher than his own head.

259
00:07:16,386 --> 00:07:17,567
This is a flood line.

260
00:07:17,623 --> 00:07:18,853
When the river floods,

261
00:07:18,873 --> 00:07:20,503
it leaves debris at the highest

262
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:21,910
point the water reached.

263
00:07:22,550 --> 00:07:24,142
Which means the whole sandbar he's

264
00:07:24,162 --> 00:07:26,275
standing on has been underwater before.

265
00:07:26,915 --> 00:07:28,096
And the driftwood that looked like

266
00:07:28,116 --> 00:07:30,120
a gift is proof the water carried

267
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:31,590
it here from somewhere else.

268
00:07:32,230 --> 00:07:33,560
Dead leaves caught in the reeds

269
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:35,636
line up at the same height too.

270
00:07:35,692 --> 00:07:37,742
Every sign points to the same answer.

271
00:07:38,382 --> 00:07:39,875
If he built his base here,

272
00:07:39,895 --> 00:07:41,050
one night of heavy rain

273
00:07:41,070 --> 00:07:42,938
could wash everything away.

274
00:07:42,995 --> 00:07:43,719
Including him.

275
00:07:44,359 --> 00:07:46,451
Lesson one: the place that looks the most

276
00:07:46,471 --> 00:07:48,634
convenient can be the most dangerous.

277
00:07:49,434 --> 00:07:51,216
Zero heads back to the meadow,

278
00:07:51,247 --> 00:07:53,447
near the big tree he saw this morning.

279
00:07:54,087 --> 00:07:55,304
The ground here is several

280
00:07:55,324 --> 00:07:57,055
meters higher than the river.

281
00:07:57,112 --> 00:07:58,343
No flood lines.

282
00:07:58,399 --> 00:07:59,611
And the soil is dry.

283
00:08:00,251 --> 00:08:01,513
But before deciding,

284
00:08:01,551 --> 00:08:03,638
he looks up and checks the branches above.

285
00:08:04,278 --> 00:08:05,083
There's a big dead

286
00:08:05,103 --> 00:08:06,527
branch hanging up there.

287
00:08:06,590 --> 00:08:07,895
Branches like that can break

288
00:08:07,915 --> 00:08:09,608
and fall at any moment,

289
00:08:09,652 --> 00:08:11,253
especially in strong wind.

290
00:08:11,893 --> 00:08:14,255
So Zero moves out from under that branch.

291
00:08:14,318 --> 00:08:15,997
He still gets afternoon shade,

292
00:08:16,017 --> 00:08:17,380
but he's not under the risk.

293
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:19,188
Just a few steps can be the

294
00:08:19,208 --> 00:08:21,195
difference between safe and hurt.

295
00:08:21,835 --> 00:08:23,828
Time for the same three questions.

296
00:08:23,885 --> 00:08:25,553
Is anything useful nearby?

297
00:08:25,610 --> 00:08:26,814
Wood from the jungle is less

298
00:08:26,834 --> 00:08:28,352
than five minutes away,

299
00:08:28,372 --> 00:08:29,647
and the river isn't far.

300
00:08:30,287 --> 00:08:31,256
Is there danger?

301
00:08:31,312 --> 00:08:32,705
He's above the flood line,

302
00:08:32,725 --> 00:08:34,229
away from falling rocks,

303
00:08:34,249 --> 00:08:36,049
and out from under the dead branch.

304
00:08:36,689 --> 00:08:37,944
If something goes wrong,

305
00:08:37,964 --> 00:08:39,133
which way does he run?

306
00:08:39,201 --> 00:08:41,157
From here he can see all around,

307
00:08:41,177 --> 00:08:42,939
and run out in any direction.

308
00:08:44,239 --> 00:08:46,131
Finally, Zero uses a stick

309
00:08:46,151 --> 00:08:48,000
to draw a map in the dirt.

310
00:08:48,063 --> 00:08:49,706
The river, the jungle,

311
00:08:49,726 --> 00:08:50,968
the cliff, and every

312
00:08:50,988 --> 00:08:52,326
danger he found today.

313
00:08:52,966 --> 00:08:54,760
Then he plants the stick right here.

314
00:08:54,816 --> 00:08:56,034
This is the very first

315
00:08:56,054 --> 00:08:57,328
base of the new world.

316
00:08:58,128 --> 00:08:59,077
From now on,

317
00:08:59,115 --> 00:09:01,153
every time he has to make a decision,

318
00:09:01,215 --> 00:09:02,747
Zero has this map:

319
00:09:02,815 --> 00:09:04,615
what's where, and what to avoid.

320
00:09:05,255 --> 00:09:06,587
So, today's lesson.

321
00:09:06,643 --> 00:09:08,023
Before you build anything,

322
00:09:08,043 --> 00:09:09,011
know the land.

323
00:09:09,068 --> 00:09:10,436
Look from high ground,

324
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:11,985
split it into directions,

325
00:09:12,005 --> 00:09:14,205
and ask three questions everywhere.

326
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:16,588
And remember: the place that looks

327
00:09:16,608 --> 00:09:18,350
most convenient is the place

328
00:09:18,370 --> 00:09:19,982
you should check most carefully.

329
00:09:20,622 --> 00:09:22,477
Unlocked: a survey map,

330
00:09:22,497 --> 00:09:23,772
and the first base site.

331
00:09:25,172 --> 00:09:26,090
But all day,

332
00:09:26,146 --> 00:09:28,553
Zero hasn't had a single drop of water.

333
00:09:28,609 --> 00:09:30,972
And the river looks so clear and tempting.

334
00:09:31,612 --> 00:09:34,006
Is water that clear really safe to drink?

335
00:09:34,062 --> 00:09:35,624
Next time, we find out.

